Map geometry
------------
public/globe-dots.bin, globe-dots-fine.bin, globe-borders.bin and
globe-coast.bin are generated by scripts/build-globe-dots.mjs and
scripts/build-globe-borders.mjs from the world-atlas package (ISC), which
packages Natural Earth 1:50m data. Natural Earth is in the public domain and
asks for no permission and no attribution; it is credited here anyway.

Photographs
-----------
The app fetches photographs at runtime from the Wikipedia REST summary
endpoint, which serves images hosted on Wikimedia Commons under their own
licences. No photograph is redistributed in this repository. Each image is
shown with the attribution the API returns; where a spot has no usable image,
the app draws a poster from the spot's own notes instead.

Weather
-------
Weather, when shown, comes from Open-Meteo (open-meteo.com), CC BY 4.0. Sun
times are computed on the client with SunCalc.

The dataset
-----------
data/research/*.json describes 604 real, publicly accessible places across 44
cities. Please read this before relying on it:

  * It is licensed CC BY 4.0 — reuse it, with attribution.

  * It is not verified. 354 of the 604 entries cite no source at all, and for
    17 cities neither the research pass nor the review pass could reach the
    web; those files say so in their own verifyNotes, in capitals. Coordinates
    are approximate and each carries its own confidence level. Opening hours
    are frequently from memory and change without notice.

  * The "safety" field is not a crime statistic, a risk score, or safety
    advice. It records physical conditions — lighting, closing time, how
    isolated a place gets after dark, terrain, water, traffic — and what to do
    about them. It is deliberately written to describe places, not the people
    in or near them. If you find an entry that fails that standard, it is a
    bug; please open an issue.

  * Nothing here should be used to decide whether an area or its residents are
    dangerous. It cannot support that, and it is not intended to.

The places are real and the descriptions are about real, named businesses and
public spaces. Corrections are welcome as issues or pull requests.
